-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner transport of Uₚ-supports, up to one diamond
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion field $\mathbb{Q}(X_1(Mp))$, let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly, and let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the $q$-expansion of $j$, assumed nonzero; $A$ and $L$ are also algebras over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$'s model $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}$, compatibly. Let $\sigma$ be an $L$-automorphism of $K$ subject to: $\sigma j$ has Laurent series $j(q^p)$; $b$ is integral over $A[j]$ if and only if $\sigma b$ is; for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $K$ consisting exactly of the $f$ with $f \cdot y = x$ for power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction, the pullback of $W_0$ along $\sigma$ differs from $W_0$ and contains $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ for every polynomial $P$ over $A$ of nonzero reduction; $\sigma$ agrees with the partial Atkin–Lehner involution `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull M p` on the elements of $K$ coming from the full modular function field of level $Mp$ (the field generated by the $j(q^d)$, $d \mid Mp$); and, for all $d, d'$ coprime to $Mp$ with $d' \equiv d \pmod M$ and $d'd \equiv 1 \pmod p$, conjugation by $\sigma$ carries any automorphism of $K$ inducing the base-changed diamond $\langle d \rangle$ to any automorphism inducing $\langle d' \rangle$. Let $\bar\sigma$ be an $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_1(Mp)) =$ `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` compatible with $\sigma$ under the coefficient extension $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume further that $y \mapsto y(q^p)$ maps $\mathbb{Q}(X_1(Mp))$ into the function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp \cdot p)$, that the two resulting $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra maps $\alpha$ (inclusion) and $\beta$ ($q \mapsto q^p$) are integral, and that the upper function field has principal divisors. Then there is a $d$ coprime to $Mp$ such that for all places $P, Q_p$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_1(Mp))$, if $Q_p$ lies in the support of the divisor correspondence $\alpha_* \beta^*$ applied to $P$, then $\bar\sigma \cdot P$ lies in the support of $\alpha_* \beta^*$ applied to $\langle d \rangle \cdot (\bar\sigma \cdot Q_p)$, the actions being those of the semilinear automorphisms attached to $\bar\sigma$ and to the base-changed diamond $\langle d \rangle$.
--
--   This is the divisorial, place-by-place form of the Atkin–Li relation $w_p U_p w_p^{-1} = \langle p \rangle^{\mp 1} U_p^{*}$ at the prime $p$ exactly dividing the level: it expresses that the partial Atkin–Lehner involution turns the $U_p$-correspondence on $X_1(Mp)$ into its transpose, after a single diamond operator uniform in the places. It feeds the subsequent analysis of the reduction of $U_p$ and of the Frobenius action on the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$.
